// Fragment_DataOps_Flow — Fragmented Data Flow in the Current Condition (DataOps)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Fragment_DataOps_Flow" (canvas name = file
//   name; the cloud architecture syntax has no title line).
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Fragment_DataOps_Flow.png
// Icons: every node carries an icon; icon names verified against
//   docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11).
// Reference: Figure III.1 (fig:fragment-dataops), Section III.1.3.
// This diagram depicts the data flow in the condition BEFORE the platform (the
// fragmented status quo): each stage uses a generic ad hoc stack assembled
// manually, so the nodes deliberately do NOT name any platform/components/
// component (the no-tools rule). Domain-agnostic: the data source names no
// particular domain.
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right), one chain left to right,
// without deep vertical stacking. Included without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Maturity basis (Section II.1.2, subsec:maturity):
// - Early stage of the DataOps evolution model (munappy2020adhoc): ad hoc
//   and semi-automated data analysis, data silos, manual pipeline monitoring.
// The "Current Maturity Characteristics" group renders that marker on the PNG.
// DELIBERATE SEPARATION: this file shares NOT ONE edge with
// Fragment_MLOps_Flow.eraser. The disconnect of the data flow from the model flow is
// its main message (the starting point of the domino effect, Section III.1.3).

direction right

// Actors
Data Engineer [icon: user, color: gray]
Business User [icon: user, color: gray]

External Data Source [icon: cloud, color: gray, label: "External Data Source (API, files, databases)"]

// Fragmented DataOps chain (left to right)
Manual Data Ingestion [icon: terminal, color: orange, label: "Manual Data Ingestion (shell scripts, CSV/FTP, email)"]
Manual Data Quality [icon: alert-triangle, color: orange, label: "Manual Data Quality (spot checks, spreadsheet review)"]
Unmanaged Data Storage [icon: database, color: orange, label: "Unmanaged Data Storage (separate databases, shared drive, object bucket)"]
Ad Hoc Reporting [icon: file-text, color: orange, label: "Ad Hoc Reporting (spreadsheet, manual report to Business User)"]

// Maturity marker (early stage of DataOps evolution), compact at the right end
Current Maturity Characteristics [icon: eye, color: gray] {
  Early DataOps Marker [icon: alert-triangle, label: "Early stage of the DataOps evolution model (munappy2020adhoc): ad hoc and semi-automated analysis, data silos, manual pipeline monitoring"]
}

// Main one-way flow, managed by the Data Engineer at each stage
External Data Source > Manual Data Ingestion: manual extraction
Data Engineer > Manual Data Ingestion: manages extraction
Manual Data Ingestion > Manual Data Quality: sporadic checks
Data Engineer > Manual Data Quality: runs checks
Manual Data Quality > Unmanaged Data Storage: validated data
Data Engineer > Unmanaged Data Storage: manages data and access
Unmanaged Data Storage > Ad Hoc Reporting: manual export
Data Engineer > Ad Hoc Reporting: compiles report
Ad Hoc Reporting > Business User: manual report delivery
